# Prompts: blindness and parity

Read `.claude/rules/prompts.md` and follow it before changing anything here.

That file is the single copy of these invariants, the ones a thesis committee probes
first: what the judge may and may not see, what the simulated user may and may not see,
the parity between `baseline` and `fsm`, prompts living in files rather than Python
strings, and the freeze at tag `v1`. Claude Code attaches it on its own through the
`paths` of its frontmatter; Cursor needs this pointer. Keeping one copy is the point, so
do not restate its rules here.
